/-- Distributions on `ℝ²` with the topology of `H^{-s}_loc`: the topology generated by the balls
`{S : ‖χ (S − T)‖²_{H^{-s}} < ε}`. It induces on `H^{-s}_loc` its usual Fréchet topology, and
`H^{-s}_loc` is a closed (not open) subset. Convergence in law in this space of random elements that
lie a.s. in `H^{-s}_loc`, with limit law carried by `H^{-s}_loc` (a Polish subspace), is equivalent to
convergence in law in `H^{-s}_loc` (portmanteau for closed sets). -/
